WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.167 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-How are you, Michael?

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm good.
I mean, it was a rough summer,

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:05.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, you know,
now we're back to school.

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:06.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not bad.
-Yeah, it's not bad to try

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:10.210
to bring a little semblanc
of normalcy into our lives

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:14.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
A thing that was very abnormal
for me is when we met.

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:18.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
We met on an Amtrak train
in 2011.

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:19.052 size:84% position:42% line:92%
We were both on our way

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
to that White House
Correspondence Dinner.

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:24.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I remember.
I remember meeting you.

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:26.860 size:78% position:39%
That was a great joy,
because I'm a fan.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.294 line:92%
But what an epic night that was.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:34.067
What a crazy --
You called out, you shot down --

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
You called out Donald Trump.
And then --

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:39.039
And then, your follow-up was
Obama calling down Donald Trump.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:42.175
And who might have guessed
where that would have gone

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:43.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
It would have been a lot nicer

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
if it had just been
a footnote of history

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
instead of a tipping point
[ Laughing ]

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:50.550
-Exactly. I mean,
that's the point where he was --

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:54.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, he started as, what,
a failed Midtown

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:56.289 size:81% position:41% line:92%
real-estate developer,

00:00:56.289 --> 00:01:01.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
then became
a successful reality-TV star

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:02.729 line:92%
which is where this happened

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:10.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now we get this bloviating
puff adder, sack of lies.

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:12.138 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What next?

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:14.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is --
It's a certainly an interestin

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:17.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
progression his career
has taken.

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:20.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
You -- You're obviously --
I think we share

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lack of fandom
for the current president.

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:26.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you're actually
taking steps with vote.org

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:29.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, really --
I guess it's sort of --

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
a bit of an online
art installation?

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:35.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that a safe way
to describe planyourvote.org

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:37.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Planyourvote --
yeah, planyourvote.org

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:40.934
was set up through vote.org,
and it's working with artist

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
to make sure that people
get out to vote

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:45.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that people plan what
they have to do in their city,

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:50.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
in their region, in their stat
to be able to vote.

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:53.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And were you always passionat
about politics,

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:59.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
or was it something that you
came to later in life?

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:01.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, it started, really,
with the band,

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.856 line:92%
with my former band, R.E.M

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:05.925 size:84% position:42%
When we were travelling
outside of the country,

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:07.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
we sudden-- this is during
the Reagan years.

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:13.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we suddenly, in Europe
were representative of America

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.268 line:92%
and people were saying --

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:17.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
we're there to play a show

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:20.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a completely unknown band,
and people were like,

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What the [bleep]
are you people thinking?

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:23.510 line:92%
What are you doing over there?

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:27.213
And so we had to, in a way
kind of politicize ourselves

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:30.517 size:78% position:39%
and educate ourselves
about who we are --

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:32.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
who we are
to the rest of the world

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:34.387 line:92%
and who we are to ourselves.

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:38.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would at least hope,
in most foreign countries,

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:39.959 line:92%
they would assume that R.E.M

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:43.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
wasn't necessarily
a Reagan band.

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:43.963 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughs ]

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:46.766
-Yeah, well, we weren't making
a whole lot of sense back then

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:50.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
Neither was he,
but people figured out

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:53.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
pretty quickly
that we were not giant fan

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
of that particular
administration.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:59.712
-You talk about not making
a lot of sense early on,

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:02.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I don't know
if I'd agree with that.

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:04.484
But you -- again, you've had
an interesting progression

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:06.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now
you're writing solo music.

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:09.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
It must be
a very strange experience,

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:12.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
having worked with a band
for so long.

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:14.494 size:81% position:41% line:92%
How have you found it?

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:18.298
-Well, I had -- for 32 years
through R.E.M., I had, you know,

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:24.804
for me, the greatest -- th
greatest possible co-writers

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
working on
and composing all the music,

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:32.011
and then my job was to listen to
what they did and respond to it.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:34.314 line:92%
I'm now composing myself,

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:37.684
and it's the first time in m
life that I've written music

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:40.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I found it
weirdly satisfying.

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:42.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't say that it sounds
very much like R.E.M.,

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:44.924 size:78% position:39%
but I'm really happy
with where it's gone.

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:48.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I've been able to,
because of R.E.M.

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:52.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
and because of all the fan
across the years,

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:53.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm able to take
all the money that I make

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:56.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the first year
of the release of every single

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:57.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I'm putting out
as a solo artist

00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:04.577
and donate it or dedicate it
to organizations and movements

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:07.080 line:92%
that I feel very strongly about,

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.515 size:81% position:41%
like Pathway to Paris,
Extinction Rebellion.

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:12.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Equal Just--
The Equal Justice Initiative

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:19.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
who have that incredible
Legacy Museum down in Alabama.

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:20.193 line:92%
And, so, that feels good.

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:23.930
I feel like, as an activist,
I'm kind of doing my part.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm trying to.
-You know, I feel like

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:29.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
some artists
found this time difficult,

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:30.603 line:92%
insofar as being creative.

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:34.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
How was it for you?
-Extremely difficult.

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:38.411
I learned that I'm a better cook
than I thought I was.

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:42.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've learned that I'm better
on my own

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:43.783 line:92%
than I ever thought I could be

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:48.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm comfortable with mysel
when I'm alone.

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:50.456 size:84% position:42% line:92%
But it's been a very --

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:55.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's been a very hard year
for everyone, I think.

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:56.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's no "I think" about it.
It's been --

00:04:56.496 --> 00:05:00.466
This has been perhaps the most
difficult year of my long life

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:04.337
-One of the most difficult
things that happened, obviously,

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:08.041 size:88% position:44%
were people -- you know,
many people losing those

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:09.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
that were dear to them,
loved ones.

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:12.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we have --
had a friend in common

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:14.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
who passed away
very sadly, Hal Willner.

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:16.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
I knew Hal
from working with him at "SNL.

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:18.217 line:92%
You knew him a lot better.

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:20.620
I will say,
he's one of those people that --

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:25.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
very selfishly,
one of my first thoughts was

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:27.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I just wish
I had talked to him more.

00:05:27.427 --> 00:05:29.562 size:78% position:39%
I just wish I'd spent
more time with him,

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:30.697 line:92%
because Hal was someone who --

00:05:30.697 --> 00:05:37.036
his wisdom and his kindnes
will be very hard to replace

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:40.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I found some, um --
I found some text messages

00:05:40.807 --> 00:05:45.278 line:92%
that I didn't return from him.

00:05:45.278 --> 00:05:49.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
You -- you can't fathom
that type of loss

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:54.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
until it's happened that
dramatically and unexpectedly.

00:05:54.487 --> 00:05:57.657 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I will say -- I'm sorry.

00:05:57.657 --> 00:05:58.524 line:92%
I really loved that guy a lot.

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:01.994
Paid me the greatest complimen
I've ever been paid in my life

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:04.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I will never forget that
for my whole life.

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:07.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
But Hal and I were
working on a project

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:10.870 line:92%
that hasn't come out yet.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.672 size:84% position:42%
And, so, the last thing
that we did together

00:06:12.672 --> 00:06:17.310
is a tribute to his best friend,
I think, Lou Reed.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:20.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, that will be released
probably very soon

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:23.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
and most certainly
as a tribute to his genius

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:27.987
-I also remember
one or two compliments from Hal,

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:29.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the thing
that you could take to the ban

00:06:29.856 --> 00:06:32.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that he meant it,
because there was no way

00:06:32.558 --> 00:06:37.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
he would waste his time
lying about a piece of art

00:06:37.697 --> 00:06:40.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
He was the great champion

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:43.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the people
that are easily overlooked

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:48.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
the artists who are not so eas
to put into categories.

00:06:48.674 --> 00:06:51.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he championed people
like myself

00:06:51.778 --> 00:06:53.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
and other people
who haven't had the succes

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:55.515 line:92%
that I've had, his entire life

00:06:55.515 --> 00:06:57.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, there's a --
there's a --

00:06:57.016 --> 00:07:00.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's a powerful
and strong legacy there.

00:07:00.019 --> 00:07:01.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, thank you so much
for sharing that.

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:05.291
I could talk about Hal all day
I could talk to you all day.

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:06.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here, Michael.

00:07:06.893 --> 00:07:08.094 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I really appreciate it.

00:07:08.094 --> 00:07:11.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Seth, thanks for having me,
and stay strong.

00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:13.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Will do.
-Vote. Vote. Vote.

00:07:13.633 --> 00:07:16.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Agreed.
Agreed on all counts.

